1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,412
Sweetheart, on Christmas morning,

2
00:00:02,412 --> 00:00:04,897
the last thing anybody wants is to

3
00:00:04,897 --> 00:00:07,747
be stuck at the stove flipping pancakes

4
00:00:07,747 --> 00:00:10,379
while everybody else opens presents.

5
00:00:10,559 --> 00:00:13,403
That's why every grandmother I knew made

6
00:00:13,403 --> 00:00:16,886
a Christmas breakfast casserole the night before.

7
00:00:17,066 --> 00:00:19,614
You put it together on Christmas Eve,

8
00:00:19,614 --> 00:00:20,922
and in the morning,

9
00:00:20,922 --> 00:00:22,987
you just slide it in the oven.

10
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:25,286
But most of them come out soggy

11
00:00:25,286 --> 00:00:26,243
in the middle,

12
00:00:26,243 --> 00:00:28,020
or dry and rubbery on top.

13
00:00:28,371 --> 00:00:31,091
So tonight I'm giving you my Christmas

14
00:00:31,091 --> 00:00:33,096
morning breakfast casserole,

15
00:00:33,096 --> 00:00:34,027
step by step,

16
00:00:34,027 --> 00:00:36,389
the one my family has eaten every

17
00:00:36,389 --> 00:00:39,110
Christmas since nineteen seventy-four.

18
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,832
And the five mistakes that ruin it.

19
00:00:42,012 --> 00:00:43,036
Stay with me,

20
00:00:43,036 --> 00:00:45,870
because the last secret is what kind

21
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:47,208
of bread you use,

22
00:00:47,208 --> 00:00:48,940
and why it has to be a

23
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,279
little bit stale.

24
00:00:50,459 --> 00:00:53,698
Most people get that exactly backwards.

25
00:00:54,048 --> 00:00:56,196
When my children were little,

26
00:00:56,196 --> 00:00:58,270
Christmas morning was chaos,

27
00:00:58,270 --> 00:00:58,715
honey.

28
00:00:58,895 --> 00:01:01,506
Paper everywhere, children screaming,

29
00:01:01,506 --> 00:01:04,257
Harold trying to put a bicycle together

30
00:01:04,257 --> 00:01:06,163
with the wrong screwdriver.

31
00:01:06,343 --> 00:01:08,144
And I was in the kitchen,

32
00:01:08,144 --> 00:01:09,441
missing all of it,

33
00:01:09,441 --> 00:01:12,252
making eggs and bacon for eight people.

34
00:01:12,432 --> 00:01:15,495
One year, Susan opened the doll she'd

35
00:01:15,495 --> 00:01:17,234
wanted for two years,

36
00:01:17,234 --> 00:01:19,386
and I didn't see her face.

37
00:01:19,566 --> 00:01:21,703
I was flipping pancakes.

38
00:01:21,883 --> 00:01:23,613
I cried in the kitchen.

39
00:01:23,963 --> 00:01:25,658
The next December,

40
00:01:25,658 --> 00:01:27,260
my neighbor, Mrs.

41
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:30,433
Kowalski, gave me her recipe for what

42
00:01:30,433 --> 00:01:32,051
she called a strata,

43
00:01:32,051 --> 00:01:35,044
an overnight egg and bread casserole.

44
00:01:35,224 --> 00:01:36,325
She said, Ruth,

45
00:01:36,325 --> 00:01:38,454
you make it on Christmas Eve,

46
00:01:38,454 --> 00:01:40,363
and you put it in the oven

47
00:01:40,363 --> 00:01:42,272
when the children wake up.

48
00:01:42,452 --> 00:01:44,954
And by the time the presents are

49
00:01:44,954 --> 00:01:46,910
open, breakfast is ready.

50
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,971
And the cook gets to watch.

51
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:52,143
It changed Christmas morning in our house

52
00:01:52,143 --> 00:01:52,726
forever.

53
00:01:53,077 --> 00:01:55,583
Casseroles like this go back to the

54
00:01:55,583 --> 00:01:58,734
frugal cooks of the early nineteen hundreds,

55
00:01:58,734 --> 00:02:01,598
honey, who never threw away stale bread.

56
00:02:01,778 --> 00:02:03,725
Soak it in eggs and milk,

57
00:02:03,725 --> 00:02:07,462
bake it, and yesterday's bread becomes breakfast

58
00:02:07,462 --> 00:02:08,396
for a crowd.

59
00:02:08,576 --> 00:02:10,557
The Italians have strata,

60
00:02:10,557 --> 00:02:12,698
the French have pain perdu.

61
00:02:12,878 --> 00:02:14,869
In a minute I'll tell you why

62
00:02:14,869 --> 00:02:17,410
the stale bread is the most important

63
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:17,754
part.

64
00:02:18,104 --> 00:02:19,148
Mrs.

65
00:02:19,328 --> 00:02:22,441
Kowalski's recipe card is still in my

66
00:02:22,441 --> 00:02:24,375
recipe box, sweetheart,

67
00:02:24,375 --> 00:02:27,572
stained with fifty years of butter and

68
00:02:27,572 --> 00:02:27,908
egg.

69
00:02:28,088 --> 00:02:30,313
Her handwriting is in pencil,

70
00:02:30,313 --> 00:02:32,460
and at the bottom she wrote,

71
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:34,915
Ruth, don't skimp on the cheese.

72
00:02:35,095 --> 00:02:36,476
I never have.

73
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:38,859
She passed in nineteen ninety-one,

74
00:02:38,859 --> 00:02:40,673
and every Christmas morning,

75
00:02:40,673 --> 00:02:42,422
when I take this out of the

76
00:02:42,422 --> 00:02:44,365
oven, I say a little thank you

77
00:02:44,365 --> 00:02:44,818
to her.

78
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:47,322
I've passed the card to my daughter

79
00:02:47,322 --> 00:02:47,587
now.

80
00:02:47,767 --> 00:02:49,451
A copy, of course.

81
00:02:49,631 --> 00:02:52,185
I'll never give away the original.

82
00:02:52,535 --> 00:02:55,101
Here's what you need for a nine

83
00:02:55,101 --> 00:02:56,425
by thirteen pan,

84
00:02:56,425 --> 00:02:58,247
which feeds about ten.

85
00:02:58,427 --> 00:03:01,093
One pound of breakfast sausage,

86
00:03:01,093 --> 00:03:03,071
or bacon, or diced ham.

87
00:03:03,251 --> 00:03:05,518
Eight cups of cubed bread,

88
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:06,827
about one loaf.

89
00:03:07,007 --> 00:03:09,526
Two cups of shredded sharp cheddar.

90
00:03:09,706 --> 00:03:10,797
Ten eggs.

91
00:03:10,977 --> 00:03:13,218
Two and a half cups of milk.

92
00:03:13,398 --> 00:03:15,721
One teaspoon of dry mustard,

93
00:03:15,721 --> 00:03:17,464
one teaspoon of salt,

94
00:03:17,464 --> 00:03:19,621
half a teaspoon of pepper.

95
00:03:19,801 --> 00:03:21,809
And a few green onions.

96
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,548
And here's mistake number one,

97
00:03:24,548 --> 00:03:26,618
the secret I promised you.

98
00:03:26,798 --> 00:03:30,014
Using soft, fresh sandwich bread.

99
00:03:30,194 --> 00:03:32,936
Fresh bread soaks up the eggs and

100
00:03:32,936 --> 00:03:34,265
turns into mush,

101
00:03:34,265 --> 00:03:35,511
like wet paper.

102
00:03:35,691 --> 00:03:37,628
You want a sturdy bread,

103
00:03:37,628 --> 00:03:39,080
like French bread,

104
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,855
sourdough, or Italian,

105
00:03:40,855 --> 00:03:42,791
and it needs to be a day

106
00:03:42,791 --> 00:03:43,679
or two old.

107
00:03:43,859 --> 00:03:45,857
Stale bread is thirsty,

108
00:03:45,857 --> 00:03:46,378
honey.

109
00:03:46,558 --> 00:03:49,269
It drinks up the custard and holds

110
00:03:49,269 --> 00:03:51,820
its shape, so every bite is soft

111
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,733
inside and crisp on top.

112
00:03:54,083 --> 00:03:55,852
If your bread is fresh,

113
00:03:55,852 --> 00:03:57,237
cut it into cubes,

114
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,546
spread them on a baking sheet,

115
00:03:59,546 --> 00:04:02,469
and bake them at three hundred degrees

116
00:04:02,469 --> 00:04:05,393
for fifteen minutes until they're dry,

117
00:04:05,393 --> 00:04:06,470
but not brown.

118
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:07,939
Let them cool.

119
00:04:08,119 --> 00:04:10,590
Or leave them out on the counter,

120
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:13,286
uncovered, all day on Christmas Eve.

121
00:04:13,466 --> 00:04:15,068
That's what I do.

122
00:04:15,248 --> 00:04:17,791
The grandchildren know not to eat the

123
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:19,647
bread cubes on the counter,

124
00:04:19,647 --> 00:04:21,366
or Grandma will get them.

125
00:04:21,717 --> 00:04:24,497
And use real sharp cheddar that you

126
00:04:24,497 --> 00:04:26,244
grate yourself, honey.

127
00:04:26,424 --> 00:04:28,870
The pre-shredded cheese in the bag is

128
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,919
coated with a powder to keep it

129
00:04:30,919 --> 00:04:33,364
from sticking, and it doesn't melt as

130
00:04:33,364 --> 00:04:33,959
smoothly.

131
00:04:34,139 --> 00:04:36,136
It turns a little grainy.

132
00:04:36,316 --> 00:04:38,914
A block of sharp cheddar costs about

133
00:04:38,914 --> 00:04:41,367
the same, and it takes two minutes

134
00:04:41,367 --> 00:04:42,017
to grate.

135
00:04:42,197 --> 00:04:44,553
Your casserole will be creamier,

136
00:04:44,553 --> 00:04:47,131
and the top will brown beautifully.

137
00:04:47,481 --> 00:04:49,728
Cook the sausage in a skillet,

138
00:04:49,728 --> 00:04:50,852
breaking it up,

139
00:04:50,852 --> 00:04:52,275
until it's browned.

140
00:04:52,455 --> 00:04:54,836
And here's mistake number two.

141
00:04:55,016 --> 00:04:56,397
Not draining it.

142
00:04:56,577 --> 00:04:58,915
All that grease sinks to the bottom

143
00:04:58,915 --> 00:05:01,320
and makes the whole thing greasy and

144
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:01,720
heavy.

145
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:04,257
Drain it well on paper towels.

146
00:05:04,437 --> 00:05:06,752
If you're adding vegetables,

147
00:05:06,752 --> 00:05:08,489
like onions, peppers,

148
00:05:08,489 --> 00:05:10,225
mushrooms or spinach,

149
00:05:10,225 --> 00:05:11,548
cook them first,

150
00:05:11,548 --> 00:05:11,879
too.

151
00:05:12,059 --> 00:05:14,742
Raw vegetables let out water as they

152
00:05:14,742 --> 00:05:17,574
bake, and that's another soggy middle.

153
00:05:17,924 --> 00:05:19,793
If this is helping you,

154
00:05:19,793 --> 00:05:21,987
tap the like button for me,

155
00:05:21,987 --> 00:05:22,881
sweetheart.

156
00:05:23,061 --> 00:05:25,871
It helps Grandma more than you know.

157
00:05:26,051 --> 00:05:28,059
Butter your baking dish well.

158
00:05:28,239 --> 00:05:30,482
Spread half the bread cubes in the

159
00:05:30,482 --> 00:05:30,944
bottom.

160
00:05:31,124 --> 00:05:33,447
Sprinkle half the sausage and half the

161
00:05:33,447 --> 00:05:34,363
cheese over it.

162
00:05:34,543 --> 00:05:36,294
Then the rest of the bread,

163
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:37,849
the rest of the sausage,

164
00:05:37,849 --> 00:05:39,729
and the rest of the cheese on

165
00:05:39,729 --> 00:05:39,989
top.

166
00:05:40,169 --> 00:05:42,846
Layers, honey, so every bite has a

167
00:05:42,846 --> 00:05:44,499
little of everything.

168
00:05:44,849 --> 00:05:46,010
In a big bowl,

169
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,254
whisk the eggs,

170
00:05:47,254 --> 00:05:50,655
milk, mustard, salt and pepper until it's

171
00:05:50,655 --> 00:05:54,057
completely smooth, with no streaks of egg

172
00:05:54,057 --> 00:05:54,554
white.

173
00:05:54,734 --> 00:05:57,863
Mistake number three is not whisking enough,

174
00:05:57,863 --> 00:06:00,566
and then you get rubbery white streaks

175
00:06:00,566 --> 00:06:01,561
of cooked egg.

176
00:06:01,741 --> 00:06:04,206
Pour it slowly and evenly over the

177
00:06:04,206 --> 00:06:05,004
whole dish.

178
00:06:05,184 --> 00:06:07,506
Then press down on the bread with

179
00:06:07,506 --> 00:06:09,054
the back of a spatula,

180
00:06:09,054 --> 00:06:10,954
so every cube gets a drink.

181
00:06:11,304 --> 00:06:12,750
Cover it with foil,

182
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:15,413
and put it in the icebox overnight.

183
00:06:15,593 --> 00:06:18,123
And that's mistake number four,

184
00:06:18,123 --> 00:06:18,612
honey.

185
00:06:18,792 --> 00:06:21,288
Not letting it sit long enough.

186
00:06:21,468 --> 00:06:23,573
It needs at least eight hours,

187
00:06:23,573 --> 00:06:25,677
so the bread soaks up all that

188
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:28,063
custard all the way to the center.

189
00:06:28,243 --> 00:06:30,050
If you bake it right away,

190
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:31,997
you get dry bread on top and

191
00:06:31,997 --> 00:06:34,291
a puddle of runny egg underneath.

192
00:06:34,471 --> 00:06:37,254
Overnight is the whole secret of the

193
00:06:37,254 --> 00:06:37,641
dish.

194
00:06:37,991 --> 00:06:40,798
And here's what I do on Christmas

195
00:06:40,798 --> 00:06:42,159
Eve, sweetheart.

196
00:06:42,339 --> 00:06:44,438
After the children are in bed,

197
00:06:44,438 --> 00:06:46,958
and the presents are under the tree,

198
00:06:46,958 --> 00:06:49,478
Harold and I would put this together

199
00:06:49,478 --> 00:06:50,948
at the kitchen table,

200
00:06:50,948 --> 00:06:53,048
with a glass of eggnog and the

201
00:06:53,048 --> 00:06:54,517
radio playing carols.

202
00:06:54,697 --> 00:06:56,427
It took twenty minutes.

203
00:06:56,607 --> 00:06:59,313
It became one of my favorite parts

204
00:06:59,313 --> 00:07:02,257
of Christmas, that quiet half hour in

205
00:07:02,257 --> 00:07:04,804
the kitchen, just the two of us.

206
00:07:05,154 --> 00:07:07,688
If you have a houseful of company,

207
00:07:07,688 --> 00:07:08,880
honey, make two.

208
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:11,802
They fit side by side in most

209
00:07:11,802 --> 00:07:12,369
ovens.

210
00:07:12,549 --> 00:07:14,792
And if you're feeding just two or

211
00:07:14,792 --> 00:07:17,239
three people, cut the recipe in half

212
00:07:17,239 --> 00:07:19,550
and use an eight-inch square dish.

213
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:22,458
It bakes about ten minutes faster.

214
00:07:22,638 --> 00:07:24,952
I make a little one for Harold's

215
00:07:24,952 --> 00:07:27,409
sister every year and take it over

216
00:07:27,409 --> 00:07:28,638
on Christmas Eve,

217
00:07:28,638 --> 00:07:31,385
so she can have Christmas breakfast in

218
00:07:31,385 --> 00:07:32,542
her own kitchen.

219
00:07:32,892 --> 00:07:34,699
So far, stale bread,

220
00:07:34,699 --> 00:07:36,867
drained sausage, layers,

221
00:07:36,867 --> 00:07:38,042
a good whisk,

222
00:07:38,042 --> 00:07:40,392
and a night in the icebox.

223
00:07:40,572 --> 00:07:41,619
In the morning,

224
00:07:41,619 --> 00:07:43,715
when the first child wakes up,

225
00:07:43,715 --> 00:07:46,230
take the casserole out of the icebox

226
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:48,256
and let it sit on the counter

227
00:07:48,256 --> 00:07:50,981
for thirty minutes while the oven heats

228
00:07:50,981 --> 00:07:52,588
to three hundred fifty.

229
00:07:52,768 --> 00:07:55,499
Mistake number five is putting it in

230
00:07:55,499 --> 00:07:56,181
ice cold.

231
00:07:56,361 --> 00:07:59,461
The outside burns before the middle cooks.

232
00:07:59,811 --> 00:08:02,298
Bake it covered with foil for thirty

233
00:08:02,298 --> 00:08:04,716
minutes, then take off the foil and

234
00:08:04,716 --> 00:08:07,342
bake another twenty to thirty minutes,

235
00:08:07,342 --> 00:08:09,691
until the top is puffed and golden

236
00:08:09,691 --> 00:08:11,833
and a knife in the center comes

237
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:12,523
out clean.

238
00:08:12,703 --> 00:08:15,459
Let it rest for ten minutes before

239
00:08:15,459 --> 00:08:17,080
cutting, so it sets.

240
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,579
And while it bakes,

241
00:08:18,579 --> 00:08:20,591
honey, you go sit by the tree

242
00:08:20,591 --> 00:08:22,672
in your bathrobe with a cup of

243
00:08:22,672 --> 00:08:25,517
coffee and watch every single present get

244
00:08:25,517 --> 00:08:26,003
opened.

245
00:08:26,353 --> 00:08:27,778
Once you know how,

246
00:08:27,778 --> 00:08:29,917
change it any way you like.

247
00:08:30,097 --> 00:08:32,732
Ham and Swiss with a little Dijon.

248
00:08:32,912 --> 00:08:36,233
Bacon and pepper jack with green chiles.

249
00:08:36,413 --> 00:08:40,174
Spinach, mushrooms and feta for the vegetarians.

250
00:08:40,354 --> 00:08:42,858
Or make a sweet one with cinnamon

251
00:08:42,858 --> 00:08:45,589
bread, cream cheese and blueberries,

252
00:08:45,589 --> 00:08:48,168
and pour maple syrup over the top.

253
00:08:48,348 --> 00:08:52,020
My grandchildren insist on two pans now,

254
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:54,315
one savory and one sweet.

255
00:08:54,666 --> 00:08:57,204
And serve it with something fresh and

256
00:08:57,204 --> 00:08:58,508
bright on the side,

257
00:08:58,508 --> 00:08:59,263
sweetheart.

258
00:08:59,443 --> 00:09:02,938
A bowl of oranges and grapefruit sections.

259
00:09:03,118 --> 00:09:06,078
A plate of sliced apples with cinnamon.

260
00:09:06,258 --> 00:09:09,079
And a pitcher of fresh orange juice.

261
00:09:09,259 --> 00:09:11,976
That's the whole Christmas breakfast,

262
00:09:11,976 --> 00:09:14,472
made ahead, with one dish to wash.

263
00:09:14,652 --> 00:09:17,281
My family has eaten it every Christmas

264
00:09:17,281 --> 00:09:18,941
morning for fifty years,

265
00:09:18,941 --> 00:09:21,154
and they'd riot if I changed it.

266
00:09:21,504 --> 00:09:24,277
And leftovers, if there are any,

267
00:09:24,277 --> 00:09:26,531
are wonderful, sweetheart.

268
00:09:26,711 --> 00:09:28,310
Cut them into squares,

269
00:09:28,310 --> 00:09:29,910
wrap each one in foil,

270
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:32,164
and keep them in the icebox for

271
00:09:32,164 --> 00:09:34,491
four days or the freezer for two

272
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:35,000
months.

273
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,911
Warm a square in the oven or

274
00:09:36,911 --> 00:09:39,261
the microwave for a quick breakfast on

275
00:09:39,261 --> 00:09:40,312
a school morning.

276
00:09:40,492 --> 00:09:43,025
My grandson takes one to work every

277
00:09:43,025 --> 00:09:45,124
day the week after Christmas.

278
00:09:45,304 --> 00:09:47,236
He says it's the best part of

279
00:09:47,236 --> 00:09:48,102
the holidays.

280
00:09:48,453 --> 00:09:50,182
So one more time.

281
00:09:50,362 --> 00:09:52,734
Use sturdy, stale bread,

282
00:09:52,734 --> 00:09:55,204
dried out if you need to.

283
00:09:55,384 --> 00:09:58,530
Drain the sausage and cook the vegetables.

284
00:09:58,710 --> 00:09:59,534
Layer it.

285
00:09:59,714 --> 00:10:02,721
Whisk the eggs until smooth and press

286
00:10:02,721 --> 00:10:03,940
the bread down.

287
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,653
Let it sit overnight.

288
00:10:05,833 --> 00:10:08,991
Thirty minutes on the counter before baking.

289
00:10:09,171 --> 00:10:11,609
Foil on, then foil off.

290
00:10:11,789 --> 00:10:14,409
And then go sit by the tree,

291
00:10:14,409 --> 00:10:14,970
honey.

292
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,195
You've earned it.

293
00:10:16,545 --> 00:10:18,463
Tell me in the comments,

294
00:10:18,463 --> 00:10:19,343
sweetheart.

295
00:10:19,523 --> 00:10:21,968
What does your family eat on Christmas

296
00:10:21,968 --> 00:10:22,483
morning?

297
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:24,277
I'd love to know.

298
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:27,477
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

299
00:10:27,477 --> 00:10:29,419
right there on your screen,

300
00:10:29,419 --> 00:10:31,433
and I'll see you in the next

301
00:10:31,433 --> 00:10:31,864
video.

302
00:10:32,044 --> 00:10:33,635
Good night, honey.

303
00:10:33,815 --> 00:10:35,254
Merry Christmas.
